\section*{Purpose}
This README describes the full build and deployment process for the
Suprakernel Sovereign Architecture. It covers cluster preparation,
dependency compilation, runtime configuration, telemetry initialization,
and sovereign kernel activation.

\section{Cluster Requirements}
\subsection{Hardware}
The architecture is validated on:
\begin{itemize}
    \item 64-node NVIDIA HGX H100 cluster,
    \item 8$\times$H100 GPUs per node,
    \item NVLink 4.0 interconnect fabric,
    \item 2 TB system RAM per node,
    \item direct-to-chip liquid cooling.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Software Stack}
Required system components:
\begin{itemize}
    \item CUDA Toolkit (12.x or later),
    \item NVIDIA PTX JIT Compiler,
    \item LLVM toolchain,
    \item RDMA-enabled MPI stack,
    \item FITS/HDFS ingestion libraries,
    \item sovereign telemetry daemon.
\end{itemize}

\section{Build Process}
\subsection{Step 1: Environment Initialization}
Load CUDA, LLVM, and MPI modules:
\begin{verbatim}
module load cuda/12
module load llvm
module load mpi
\end{verbatim}

Initialize sovereign environment variables:
\begin{verbatim}
export SK_ROOT=/opt/suprakernel
export SK_TELEMETRY=/var/sk/telemetry
export SK_CLUSTER_CONFIG=config/cluster.yaml
\end{verbatim}

\subsection{Step 2: Core Compilation}
Compile the sovereign execution core:
\begin{verbatim}
make sovereign-core
\end{verbatim}

Compile the manifold solver:
\begin{verbatim}
make manifold-solver
\end{verbatim}

Compile the autonomous mutation engine:
\begin{verbatim}
make autodidact-loop
\end{verbatim}

\subsection{Step 3: PTX Kernel Generation}
Generate initial CUDA/PTX kernels:
\begin{verbatim}
make kernels
\end{verbatim}

All kernels are validated against Lyapunov and CBF constraints before
activation.

\section{Runtime Configuration}
\subsection{Telemetry Daemon}
Start the sovereign telemetry daemon:
\begin{verbatim}
sk-telemetryd --config $SK_CLUSTER_CONFIG
\end{verbatim}

This daemon monitors:
\begin{itemize}
    \item tensor core utilization,
    \item Jacobian determinant $J(p)$,
    \item Lyapunov margin $(\alpha - \beta)$,
    \item memory bandwidth saturation,
    \item ingestion buffer pressure.
\end{itemize}

\subsection{Manifold Initialization}
Initialize the Riemannian stress manifold:
\begin{verbatim}
sk-manifold-init --omega-map config/omega.yaml
\end{verbatim}

\section{Sovereign Kernel Activation}
Activate the autonomous kernel:
\begin{verbatim}
sk-activate --loop autodidact
\end{verbatim}

The four-stage cycle begins:
\[
\text{Observe} \rightarrow \text{Orient} \rightarrow \text{Mutate} \rightarrow \text{Verify}.
\]

All mutations $\Delta K$ must satisfy:
\begin{equation}
\dot{L}(p) < 0, \qquad
J(p) > 0, \qquad
\dot{h}(p) + \gamma_{\text{CBF}} h(p) \ge 0.
\end{equation}

\section{Cluster Deployment}
Launch the suprakernel across all nodes:
\begin{verbatim}
mpirun -np 64 sk-node --sovereign
\end{verbatim}

Each node performs:
\begin{itemize}
    \item local manifold projection,
    \item distributed Lyapunov evaluation,
    \item synchronized mutation verification,
    \item telemetry aggregation.
\end{itemize}

